ction with momentum and rubber-band bounds. The draggable","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"card responds to touch input via Origami’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"origami.Drag"},{"text":" patch, which wires its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"output ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Position"},{"text":" to the layer’s transform. When released near the center, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"card snaps back to its resting position.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Interaction_DragView","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview","title":"Interaction_DragView","type":"topic"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView/alignmentGuide(_:computeValue:)-4ccvv":{"title":"alignmentGuide(_:computeValue:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"alignmentGuide","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"HorizontalAlignment","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI19HorizontalAlignmentV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"computeValue","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"ViewDimensions","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI14ViewDimensionsV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CGFloat","preciseIdentifier":"s:14CoreFoundation7CGFloatV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"View","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI4ViewP","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview\/alignmentguide(_:computevalue:)-4ccvv","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView\/alignmentGuide(_:computeValue:)-4ccvv","abstract":[]},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"type":"topic","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"Swami","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"code":".origami","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"}}}